@page "/security"
@layout LTSFrontend.Layout.PublicPageLayout

<PageTitle>Security - Litigation Tracking System</PageTitle>

<section class="public-page-hero">
    <span class="eyebrow">Security &amp; Compliance</span>
    <h1>Bank-Level Security for Privileged Legal Data</h1>
    <p>
        Litigation records are among the most sensitive documents a firm holds. LTS is built
        with authentication, authorization, and audit controls at every layer.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="public-page-body">

    <div class="public-feature-grid">
        <div class="public-feature-card">
            <div class="icon-wrap"><i class="bi bi-key"></i></div>
            <h3>JWT-Based Authentication</h3>
            <p>Every session is secured with a signed JWT token embedding the user's firm and role, over HTTPS.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="public-feature-card">
            <div class="icon-wrap"><i class="bi bi-diagram-3"></i></div>
            <h3>Role-Based Access Control</h3>
            <p>Permissions are enforced dynamically across the full role hierarchy, from Super Admin down to Intern.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="public-feature-card">
            <div class="icon-wrap"><i class="bi bi-building-lock"></i></div>
            <h3>Row-Level, Multi-Tenant Isolation</h3>
            <p>Every database query is filtered by Firm ID, so one firm can never access another firm's cases &mdash; even by guessing a URL.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="public-feature-card">
            <div class="icon-wrap"><i class="bi bi-eye-slash"></i></div>
            <h3>Conditional Document Access</h3>
            <p>Restricted-mode Moharrir uploads go through a write-only endpoint; view/download stay disabled until elevated.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="public-feature-card">
            <div class="icon-wrap"><i class="bi bi-clock-history"></i></div>
            <h3>Complete Audit Logging</h3>
            <p>Every create, update, delete, login, and permission change is logged with user, timestamp, and old/new values.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="public-feature-card">
            <div class="icon-wrap"><i class="bi bi-hourglass-split"></i></div>
            <h3>Session &amp; Timeout Controls</h3>
            <p>Sessions expire automatically after inactivity, and old sessions are invalidated immediately after logout.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="public-feature-card">
            <div class="icon-wrap"><i class="bi bi-shield-lock"></i></div>
            <h3>Encrypted Credentials</h3>
            <p>Passwords are hashed (bcrypt/SHA-based) and never stored or transmitted in plain text.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="public-feature-card">
            <div class="icon-wrap"><i class="bi bi-file-earmark-lock"></i></div>
            <h3>Document-Level Permissions</h3>
            <p>View, download, upload, delete, and print rights can be set per role or per user, per document.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="public-feature-card">
            <div class="icon-wrap"><i class="bi bi-database-lock"></i></div>
            <h3>No Direct Database Access</h3>
            <p>All access goes through the authenticated, permission-checked API &mdash; never direct client-to-database queries.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="public-split-row">
        <div>
            <div class="public-section-title" style="text-align:left; margin:0 0 1.5rem;">
                <span class="eyebrow">Defense in Depth</span>
                <h2>Unauthorized Access Is Denied at Every Layer</h2>
            </div>
            <ul class="public-check-list">
                <li>
                    <i class="bi bi-check-lg"></i>
                    <div>
                        <h4>Blocked at the URL Level</h4>
                        <p>Changing a URL to try to reach another case, firm, or document is rejected server-side, not just hidden in the UI.</p>
                    </div>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <i class="bi bi-check-lg"></i>
                    <div>
                        <h4>Protected Against Brute Force</h4>
                        <p>Repeated failed logins trigger lockout / protective measures on the account.</p>
                    </div>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <i class="bi bi-check-lg"></i>
                    <div>
                        <h4>Input Validation &amp; Sanitization</h4>
                        <p>All search and form inputs are safely handled to prevent injection-based attacks.</p>
                    </div>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <i class="bi bi-check-lg"></i>
                    <div>
                        <h4>Firm Blocking &amp; Offboarding</h4>
                        <p>Super Admins can instantly block a firm's workspace, suspending all of that firm's users at once.</p>
                    </div>
                </li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="public-panel">
            <h4 style="color:var(--lts-navy); font-weight:700; margin-bottom:1rem;">Security Test Coverage</h4>
            <ul class="public-check-list">
                <li><i class="bi bi-shield-check"></i><div><p style="margin:0;">Access denied without login</p></div></li>
                <li><i class="bi bi-shield-check"></i><div><p style="margin:0;">Cross-firm / cross-case access denied</p></div></li>
                <li><i class="bi bi-shield-check"></i><div><p style="margin:0;">SQL injection attempts safely handled</p></div></li>
                <li><i class="bi bi-shield-check"></i><div><p style="margin:0;">Session invalidated after logout</p></div></li>
                <li><i class="bi bi-shield-check"></i><div><p style="margin:0;">Admin functions blocked for normal users</p></div></li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="public-cta-banner">
        <h2>Have Security or Compliance Questions?</h2>
        <p>Talk to us about how LTS fits your firm's data protection requirements.</p>
        <a href="/contact" class="btn-gold">Contact Our Team</a>
    </div>

</section>
